# arcana-arca-payout.timer — runs the $ARCA creator payout batch once a day.
#
# CADENCE: daily at 10:00 UTC (17:00 WIB). §10.3 allows daily or weekly.
#
# Daily, because the batching that keeps gas down is per creator per run, not
# per run frequency: a creator with twenty sales still receives exactly one
# transfer per run either way. Weekly would cut the gas bill by at most 6/7 of
# an already small number while making every creator wait up to a week for
# money that is already sitting in the treasury. Creator trust is worth more
# than that. Revisit if creator count grows enough that one transfer each per
# day is itself the cost.
#
# The hour puts the run in the WIB afternoon: this moves real funds, and a
# failure needs a person, not a 3am alert nobody reads. One hour after the
# reminder job so the two never overlap.
#
# To switch to weekly: OnCalendar=Mon *-*-* 10:00:00 UTC
#
# Persistent=true: a missed run fires at the next boot. Creators are owed the
# money either way and the batch is idempotent per payment_event.
[Unit]
Description=Run the ARCANA $ARCA creator payout batch daily

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 10:00:00 UTC
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
